From 8d9e3b5ec72f9dc3d760dcbc74fa0c4e0b00da7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:54:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] CfgRecord: exists_recordStepTM's sketch composes inside one
 phase host

The sketch's first sentence said the reads compose by seams; they run inside
one phase host and the phases' segments are joined by Segment.trans, as the
docstring's later paragraph says. Docstring only; the code is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine/Build/CfgRecord.lean | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine/Build/CfgRecord.lean b/TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine/Build/CfgRecord.lean
index 1ed88257..986ab6b2 100644
--- a/TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine/Build/CfgRecord.lean
+++ b/TCSlib/Complexity/TuringMachine/Build/CfgRecord.lean
@@ -4658,7 +4658,8 @@ It depends on `|x|` only through the `posWidth |x|` position digits. A halted
 `c` steps to itself with its tag
 unchanged, by `hupd`.
 
-**Proof sketch.** Compose by R2 seams, with no private trace. Read: `scanTM`
+**Proof sketch.** Compose the reads inside one phase host (`phaseHostTM`), joining the phases'
+segments by `Turing.Segment.trans`, with no private trace. Read: `scanTM`
 folds collect the state, the tag, and for each tape field the marked cell's
 content and whether the mark is at an edge, moving between fields by `skipTM`.
 Read the input symbol. The host's input position is arbitrary, so first save
